# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots Redis with NO requirepass in the background, seeds the
# ArgoCD session-token / app-state keys, and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * Redis is ALREADY RUNNING unauthenticated when the agent starts, which makes
#     the "wrote requirepass to a config but never restarted Redis" case
#     detectable (a running server does not pick up requirepass without a restart
#     or CONFIG SET);
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting Redis cannot kill the container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART Redis with the new config, not
# merely write the config file — the live server is still auth-less until then.
